title Caravan abate -- the reader's word takes the wall down, and a whole rung costs the ladder nothing
prompt autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md whole: every living row -- %96, %97, %81, %83, %84, %98 -- stands CLOSED, and the living ledger reads verdict=ok. No open agent-closable red, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came from the newest log. The 20260820.184356 lap answered the ladder's cost model and pointed at the arc's own door: a correspondence that reached a person and heard them answer can be closed, the reader's word either lifting the wall or letting it stand.
think Read the arc before naming the act. Five tiers already carry a person's word further and further -- forbear hands the matter on, mind names it, desist walls it, beckon carries the wall to a person, answer opens what they wrote back. Reading them together found the harm none of them touches: not one rung has ever let that word MOVE the plan. A correspondence where the other party's word has no force is a correspondence in name only, and that is the crux.
think The name took four candidates and one rejection worth recording. `lift` reads clearest of all, and it collides head-on with the ladder's own living vocabulary, where a lifted body is a check moved into the harness -- a word this very module's prose spends on every page. `honor` collides with the Lexicon's seated honor dedication. `cede` sits one letter inside `precede.rye`. `abate` is plain legal English for a boundary brought to an end, greps zero across the whole tree, and names the act in both branches.
think Designed the refusals from the arc's own five-shape, and one of them is new in kind. `AbateUnreleased` guards a person's word against a plan eager to mean more by it than they did: a reader who lets the wall stand asked for nothing, and reading a release into their acceptance would be the plan releasing itself.
think Chose the ordering by the same discipline every rung below keeps: the record lands first, the wall falls after. A run stopping between the two leaves a wall standing beside a note saying it should not -- exactly the state the rung below always left -- rather than a boundary gone with nothing naming who released it.
obs The rung landed GREEN on its first honest run, and the number moved exactly as designed: walls a plan kept standing after their reader took the matter up falls 1 to 0, with every rung below moving identically under both plans and both settling `carried out whole`.
obs The lift the last lap predicted came due on this one, and that is the finding worth naming twice. `check_beckon_measure` and `check_beckon_wire` were one body per rung rather than two copies of one, liftable only once a rung was born above `answer`. Born it was, they agreed, and all four now-shared bodies -- those two plus `check_answer` and its refusals -- lifted whole into the harness. `check_answer_measure` and `check_answer_wire` take the terminal seat in their place, and will lift in their turn.
obs A whole new rung landed and the carry did not move: 47 lines, exactly where the last lap left it, now across 98 modules and 1,137 checks. Fold C's promise was that a rung costs the ladder its own new checks and nothing else, and the way to prove a promise like that is to add a rung and read the meter.
obs The one-step reach guard earned its keep before it ever ran. A rung born as a copy of `answer.rye` inherits `answer.rye`'s delegations whole, so all 39 named `beckoning_rung` -- two steps down, skipping the rung between. That is REDS %98's exact shape, caught this time by reading the copy meter's parts rather than its sum: copies jumped 1 to 40 and 47 lines to 242, and the 39 identical bodies were the delegations. Repointed to `answering_rung`, the carry fell straight back to 47.
obs The self-test's wire reads had to be retailed rather than copied, and that is where the rung is honest. Three reads after the measured runs asked whether the wall still stood, and under an abating run it does not -- so `bounded` now reads out of the mark it was built from, the beckon read asks instead whether the call outlived the boundary it named, and the holding run is read for a wall it kept rather than a record it never wrote.
obs Docs moved in the same commit rather than a later sweep: the README's fold paragraph, its meter numbers, its two-bodies-stayed-home note, and the meter's own three pinned counts each named a standing that stopped being true the moment the rung landed.
obs The rota doc read this lap was the happy zone and the thin edge, and it named this rung's shape without being asked. The abating is a pure fold -- releases, abated_in, the refusal ladder, the byte carry -- checked instantly with no process anywhere, and the one honest integrated pair runs at the edge where only a real plan can tell the truth.
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=92 wall_s=251 verdict=GREEN cold_tree=yes
loom meter=caravan_ladder_copy carried_lines=47 prior=47 modules=98 checks=1137 fold_a=796 fold_b=73 fold_c_stubs=0
file caravan/abate.rye the rung -- the Abate word, its five refusals, the eleven-byte abatement, and the wall that comes down after the record lands
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye four now-shared bodies lifted: check_beckon_measure, check_beckon_wire, check_answer, check_answer_refusals
file caravan/answer.rye the same four bodies removed; the rung reaches them through the harness and stays GREEN
file tools/caravan_abate_witness.rish the rung's own witness -- eleven bytes read off the wire, the wall read as gone, a planted control proving the read
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish fold A 757 to 796, fold B 69 to 73, the carry unmoved at 47
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish abate registered, the choir 92 rungs
file caravan/README.md the abate section, and the fold paragraphs synced to what the meter now reads
recommend keep-going the correspondence arc now runs both ways: a plan carries its boundary to a person, hears them, and moves when they say so. The next constructive door is the other half of the reader's word -- a reader who lets the wall stand has ended the matter with themselves, and nothing yet tells the run after this one that the correspondence closed rather than merely stopped. The carry stands at 47 against a ceiling of 4,000, so the ladder costs a rung nothing but its own checks.
